APPROVE

**Reasons**
No blocking findings.

- Closest-first traversal is correct: [discoSemanticResolver.ts:37](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:37) applies within-node specificity, and [line 72](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:72) walks from `start` upward. A farther `section`/`file` cannot mask a closer valid `indexed`/`field`/`comment_anchor`.
- `break` control flow is correct for invalid indexed metadata and section-less fields: by the time [lines 79](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:79) or [89](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:89) run, all closer descendants have already been inspected. Breaking prevents farther semantic ancestors from winning, then [sourceFallback](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:56) finds the nearest parseable `data-oid`.
- Type split is clean: `DiscoResolvedTarget = DiscoSemanticTarget | SourceRef` at [line 33](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:33), `SourceRef.kind === "source"` at [selectionBridge.ts:33](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/selectionBridge.ts:33), and `semanticEditTarget` only accepts `DiscoSemanticTarget` at [line 108](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/frontend/src/lib/resolvers/discoSemanticResolver.ts:108).
- Drift guard correctly enforces exact equality of DOM attribute string values via set comparison at [test_semantic_attr_parity.py:17](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/packages/core/tests/test_semantic_attr_parity.py:17). Caveat: it does not catch TS constant key renames if the string values stay identical, but that is outside the stated value-parity contract.
- DOM walk looks fine for detached elements and SVG elements because it uses `Element` APIs. Text nodes are not accepted by the function signature; callers with a generic `Node` must normalize to an `Element` first.

**Required Revisions**
None.

**Non-Blocking Test Gaps**
I would add regression tests for invalid indexed metadata inside a valid section resolving to source fallback, and a field inside a file wrapper without any section resolving to source fallback instead of the file. Also replace the test-only `semanticEditTarget(t as never)` casts with an `isSemanticTarget` branch so the intended narrowing path is covered.
